// The played bed with a thicket -- M2's question, 2026-09-10.
//
// `played_bed.ron` is the owner's mix (grass, herb, shrub) and it has no LOW
// fruiting plant: herb's flowers and fruit stand 22-40 rows up a stem, so
// the loop "an ant bites a fallen fruit" almost never fires -- measured on
// PR #301, **two bites in 360,000 frames** across three seeds
// (`Reports/dead-ends.md` line 1636's finding, reproduced independently).
// `scrambler` (`assets/species/scrambler.ron`) is a sprawling determinate
// thicket that carries flowers and fruit at ground level at every axis end
// -- exactly the shape the played bed is missing. This file is the played
// bed with four scramblers added, everything else byte-identical, so a
// difference in the mechanism's counters is attributable to the thicket and
// nothing else.
//
// **Four columns, chosen to keep the mix and stay off two things**: the
// existing thirteen placements (grass/herb/shrub at x in {25, 50, 75, 105,
// 130, 155, 180, 330, 355, 380, 410, 435, 465}) and, more importantly,
// `played_bed.ron`'s own nest band, columns 210..310, which that file's own
// header explains must stay bare of founders or `found_colony_of` seats a
// colony of 8 instead of ~13-33 (measured there, not re-derived here). A
// scrambler standing in the band at frame 6,000 would cost the same
// founders the empty band exists to protect, so the four go at 15, 195,
// 315 and 495 -- bracketing the band from outside it rather than the
// 90/215/300/490 first sketched, which put two of the four inside it.
//
// **Nothing else differs.** Same bed size, same soil/ground/lamp geometry,
// same seed, same colony timeline at frame 6,000. A finding here is a
// finding about the thicket, not about a second confound riding along with
// it -- the sibling of the played-bed file's own "prove the edit touched
// only its target" discipline.
(
    name: "played_bed_scrambler",
    title: "THE PLAYED BED WITH A THICKET",
    question: "The owner's mix plus scrambler, a low fruiting thicket at ground level -- does fruit reach the floor, do ants bite it, and does the colony eat better for it?",
    bed: (
        width: 512,
        height: 320,
        soil_depth: 80,
        ground_y: 160,
        compartments: 1,
        founders: 0,
        species: "grass",
        colonies: 0,
        colony_ants: 52,
        colony_species: "ant",
        predators: 0,
        lamp_spacing: 33,
        seed: 1,
        extra_walls: [],
    ),
    settings: [],
    placements: [
        Plant(species: "grass",     x: 25),
        Plant(species: "herb",      x: 50),
        Plant(species: "shrub",     x: 75),
        Plant(species: "grass",     x: 105),
        Plant(species: "herb",     x: 130),
        Plant(species: "grass",     x: 155),
        Plant(species: "shrub",    x: 180),
        // The four added scramblers -- see the header for why these
        // columns and not the first sketch.
        Plant(species: "scrambler", x: 15),
        Plant(species: "scrambler", x: 195),
        Plant(species: "scrambler", x: 315),
        Plant(species: "scrambler", x: 495),
        Plant(species: "grass",    x: 330),
        Plant(species: "herb",     x: 355),
        Plant(species: "shrub",    x: 380),
        Plant(species: "grass",    x: 410),
        Plant(species: "herb",     x: 435),
        Plant(species: "grass",    x: 465),
    ],
    timeline: [
        // Identical to `played_bed.ron`'s own timeline entry -- see that
        // file's header for why the band must stay bare rather than being
        // swept with an explicit `Clear`.
        (at: 6000, every: 0, until: 0, what: Colony(species: "ant", x: 256, count: 52)),
    ],
    horizon: 120000,
)
